    "Your watch was most likely off on October 2, but the summary tool is inconsistent about that day, so the answer depends on how you count it.\n\n- **October 1:** No step data at all.\n- **October 2:** 0 steps. The tool flagged this as a no-wear day and excluded it.\n- **October 3:** 6,000 steps.\n\nThe tool's headline average is **3,000 steps per day**. That figure treats October 2's zero as a real day. If you exclude October 2 as no-wear, the only valid day is October 3, at **6,000 steps**.\n\nNeither figure is a true three-day average, because October 1 has no data. If you wore the watch all day on October 1, it may not have synced yet. You can run a sync and ask again."
